--- A collection builtin is one runtime function over its items, called
--- by both modes (docs/bug-classes.md §4). Records and maps compare field
--- by field and entry by entry (compiled, two records did not compare, and
--- the interpreter answered false for both); sort puts NaN last (it had
--- sorted to where the NaN stood); an int kept in a list of floats is a
--- float; an item pushed onto a list whose items can fail is one that did
--- not. A JSON number has no length: the same refusal stops both modes
--- (compiled, its length was 0).
struct P [x, y]
ps = [P[1, 2], P[3, 4]]
log[P[1, 2] eq P[1, 2]]
log[P[3, 4] in ps]
log[P[3, 5] in ps]
log[map[k = 1] eq map[k = 1]]
xs = []
xs = push[xs, 2.5]
xs = push[xs, float['nan']]
xs = push[xs, -1.0]
xs = push[xs, 2]
log[sort[xs]]
log[2 in xs]
nums = for s in ['1', 'b']
    int[s]
nums = push[nums, 7]
log[nums]
log[7 in nums]
m = map[b = 2, a = 1]
m = set[m, 'c', 3]
m = del[m, 'b']
log[keys[m]]
log[values[m]]
log[len[m]]
log[sort[['b', 'a', 'B']]]
log[reverse['héllo']]
log[slice[[1, 2, 3, 4], -2, 10]]
j = json['{"a": [1, 2, 3], "n": 5}']
log[len[j.a]]
log[len[j.n]]
log['not reached']
